# HDPI-8424 "Send notification to claimant(s)": return name | email body, word for word from the ticket.
Warrant Withdrawn | The warrant has been withdrawn following your request that no further action be taken to enforce it. The warrant has been filed away.
No reply to request for additional information | We have not received a reply to our request for additional information. An eviction appointment will not be scheduled and the warrant has been filed away.
Eviction unsuccessful - other | The bailiff has been unable to execute the warrant [reason from the additional details free textbox to be populated here]. The warrant has been filed away.
No Claimant or agent in attendance for eviction | The bailiff attended the property as arranged, but you or your agent were not in attendance. The warrant could not be executed and has been closed.
Warrant  Issued In Error | The warrant was issued in error. No further action will be taken on this warrant and it has been filed away.
Reopen Warrant | The warrant has been reopened. The bailiff will set a new eviction date in due course using the existing warrant details.
Claimant Advised Defendant in Breathing Space | No further action will be taken by the court on this warrant while a Breathing Space Moratorium or Mental Health Crisis Moratorium is ongoing. When you notify the court that the moratorium has ended or been cancelled, you may ask the court to reschedule the eviction date at the same time.
Application Unsuccessful & Warrant returned to bailiff | The application about which you were notified was unsuccessful. If you have not yet received a copy of the court order, it will be sent to you shortly. The bailiff will continue to execute the warrant.
Request for additional information | The bailiff has been unable to identify or locate the address provided. The bailiff cannot take further action unless you provide information that allows the warrant to proceed, such as the precise location of the premises or another address. Please reply within 14 days. If you do not reply, the warrant will be closed and you will have to pay a fee to re-issue it.
Other Interim Return | The bailiff has made a return on the warrant. The reason provided by the bailiff is: [reason from the additional details free textbox to be populated here]. The court will take the next action required on the warrant.
Defendant States they are in Breathing Space (Standard or Mental Health) | The defendant has informed the court that they are in a Breathing Space Moratorium or Mental Health Crisis Moratorium. Action on this warrant has been paused. Any appointment date within the moratorium period will not go ahead. Please confirm in writing within 7 days, or before the eviction date if sooner, whether this is correct. If we do not hear from you, we will take no further action on this warrant while the moratorium is treated as ongoing.
Warrant Expired | The warrant has expired because it is more than 12 months since it was issued. The bailiff has been unable to execute the warrant during that period, and the warrant is no longer live. The bailiff cannot continue enforcement action on this warrant.
Unable to gain access to the property | The bailiff has been unable to gain access to the property because access is gated, security controlled, or otherwise restricted. The warrant could not be executed and has been closed.
Claimant did not confirm eviction | You did not confirm that you or your agent could attend the eviction. The warrant could not be executed and has been withdrawn.
No Locksmith in attendance (Claimant failed to arrange) | You did not arrange for a locksmith to attend the eviction. The warrant could not be executed and has been filed away.
No animal handler in attendance (Claimant failed to arrange) | You did not arrange for an animal handler to attend the eviction. The warrant could not be executed and has been filed away.
No animal handler in attendance (Parties unaware of animal) | The bailiff was unable to execute the warrant because an animal handler was required at the property and had not been arranged. The eviction will need to be rescheduled once suitable arrangements have been made.
No Police Presence (Police refused to attend when asked to) | The bailiff was unable to execute the warrant because police attendance was required but the police were unable or unwilling to attend. The eviction will need to be rescheduled when safe arrangements can be made.
Children Left unattended in Property | The bailiff was unable to execute the warrant because children were left unattended at the property. The eviction will need to be rescheduled when safe and appropriate arrangements can be made.
Crowds or protests. | The bailiff was unable to execute the warrant because crowds or protests at the property prevented enforcement from taking place safely. The eviction will need to be rescheduled when safe arrangements can be made.
Obstruction by defendants | The bailiff was unable to execute the warrant because the defendant or other occupiers obstructed enforcement. The eviction will need to be rescheduled when safe arrangements can be made.
Safeguarding or vulnerability concerns | The bailiff was unable to execute the warrant because safeguarding or vulnerability concerns were identified at the property. The court will consider the next appropriate action before enforcement continues.
